**Known environment gotchas hit this session:**
- `mcp__prose__search_logs` **IGNORES its query and limit** — always returns the same recent tail.
  Useful only for reading what just happened; burns ~15k tokens per call.
- `mcp__prose__list_books` ignored `universe: gutenberg` and returned GLMZ books (stale MCP schema,
  as the startup hook warns). Use the CLI with `--universe`.
- First `--calibrate-obligations` attempt failed with a **SQL `Execution Timeout Expired`** inside
  `ResetLedgerAsync` (before any LLM spend, nothing mutated — coverage still read 12/17). A plain
  retry succeeded. Suspected lock contention with the Hub's background sweeps. If it recurs it is a
  real defect: give the reset its own command timeout.

## Open questions / pending

- **Offered, unanswered: pull the raw extraction for beat 3 and find out why it opened nothing.**
- **The author's call, not mine: should the bar change?** Specifically whether "outstanding at the
  end of a text that is one third of a story" should count as a control false positive at all.
  `Score.ControlByRule` / `ControlStillOpen` / `ControlStructural` now make the two distinguishable;
  `MeetsBar` still counts them together.
- GCSH has NOT been re-read under v7. Its 41 unread beats and every precision number from it remain
  void. `--obligations coverage --slug GCSH` and `--obligations candidates` are free and unrun.
- Run 7 on GCSH not started. Not obviously the right next spend given the bar question above.

