   `dotnet run --project v3\Prose.Cli -- --obligations rescan --slug GCTOC --beat-id 01a0a69fefd372959f501b3b691dd807 --force --universe gutenberg`
   then read the Hub log tail for the `Obligation scan beat` line and any `UNREAD` warning.
2. Free, unrun: `dotnet run --project v3\Prose.Cli -- --obligations coverage --slug GCSH --universe gutenberg`
   — confirms whether GCSH's 41 unread beats were the over-length ones.
3. Free, unrun: `--obligations candidates --id <guid> --payoff-beat <guid>` on a GCSH
   "payoff not recognised" row, to separate retrieval budget from recognition.
4. Do NOT buy run 7 until the bar question is settled — every precision number it produces is
   measured against a target that penalises correct behaviour on a novel.

